                <head>215. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>The United States and the United Kingdom concluded an agreement on grain imports
                    by an exchange of notes between Ambassador David K.E. Bruce
                    and the Earl of Dundee, British Minister of State for Foreign Affairs, in London
                    on April 15, 1964. The agreement entered into force on the same date. For text,
                    see 15 UST 541; TIAS 5581. For Special
                    Representative Herter’s statement of
                    April 16 announcing the agreement, see Department of State <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, May 4, 1964, pages 703–704. Additional
                    documentation on the negotiations leading to this agreement is in Department of
                    State, Central Files, INCO–GRAINS 17 UK-US.</p>
            </div>
